{"bank_version":"expanded-candidate-12","prior_own_read_version":"expanded-candidate-10","question_count":165,"raw_key_fact_count":535,"new_or_changed_complete_entries":[{"id":"Q033","question":{"id":"Q033","question":"For Gambler, state the eligible player role, whether use is optional or mandatory, and its phase(s); then explain when does Bluff act relative to the opponent's reveal, what is announced, what happens if unchallenged, and on challenge who loses how many ships from which locations and how is the encounter then resolved? State the printed incompatible alien."},"key":{"id":"Q033","required_facts":["Role: Main player only; use: Optional.","Phase(s): Reveal.","After opponent reveals encounter card may keep own facedown, stating what it is; may lie.","If opponent does not challenge, conclude encounter as if statement true; place own encounter card facedown on bottom of deck instead of discarding.","If challenged reveal own card. If you lied, lose as many ships to warp as you had in encounter. If truth, opponent loses as many ships as opponent had in encounter.","Those lost ships MAY NOT be ships involved in encounter. Afterwards conclude normally using revealed cards.","Do not use with Sorcerer.","The losing player chooses ships under their control outside the encounter, ordinarily ships on their colonies in this original-base scope."],"contextual_background":[],"source_references":["Printed original Gambler sheet (e4f84277ff1af01bc8b6615bcf22e758ba2c460816967fb5266017e09bdd0565)","2018 FAQ p5 extraction lines419–423 and450–453; original Gambler sheet excludes ships involved in the encounter."]}},{"id":"Q104","question":{"id":"Q104","question":"After being played once, do Anti-Matter Super, Cudgel Super, Kamikaze Super, Machine Super, Masochist Super, Miser Super, or Machine Wild automatically apply in later encounters, or must the corresponding flare be played again each encounter its effect is desired? For otherwise legal uses, what timing phrases does the official FAQ quote for the effects of Kamikaze Super, Machine Super, Masochist Super, Miser Super and Cudgel Super? For the first three, does the quoted wording refer to every player's Regroup or to the user's own Regroup phases?"},"key":{"id":"Q104","required_facts":["Each listed flare must be played in each encounter in which its effect is desired; none becomes an automatic persistent effect for later encounters merely from one play.","Kamikaze Super, Machine Super and Masochist Super quote during each of your Regroup phases: the user's own Regroup phases, not every player's.","Miser Super quotes at the start of each of your encounters.","Cudgel Super quotes whenever you use your power."],"contextual_background":["These are the quoted effect timing/owner/event clauses, not a reconstruction of when the flare may first be placed faceup or of its absent full effect, role, prerequisites, cost or target. Miser's start-of-each-own-encounter wording is not relabeled as the once-per-turn Start Turn step."],"source_references":["extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp10 extraction lines969–972 (FAQ-Q148)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp12 extraction lines1125–1127 (FAQ-Q185)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp16 extraction lines1470–1473 (FAQ-Q264)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp16 extraction lines1551–1554 (FAQ-Q280)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp17 extraction lines1559–1561 (FAQ-Q281)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp17 extraction lines1581–1584 (FAQ-Q285)","extracted/cosmic-encounter-faq.txt PDF pp18 extraction lines1653–1656 (FAQ-Q303)","2018 FAQ p16 extraction1470–1473/1551–1554; p17 1581–1584; p18 1653–1656; p12 1125–1127."]}},{"id":"Q151","question":{"id":"Q151","question":"In an ordinary encounter, what opponent and system choices does a wild destiny card permit, how does a special destiny card determine the defense and location, what color does a special count as for color-sensitive effects, and do hazard symbols change base play? For the special destiny card illustrated on page7 of the original rulebook, what criterion selects the defense, may the offense qualify, how are ties broken, and where must the encounter take place?"},"key":{"id":"Q151","required_facts":["Wild permits choosing another player, encountered in that player's home system.","Special states defense conditions and location; follow its text.","For effects special is treated as the designated defense's color.","Hazard symbols have no effect in this original base game.","Select the player with the most current foreign colonies.","The offense itself is excluded.","Break a tie to the offense's left: use the first tied eligible player in that direction.","The encounter takes place in the selected other player's home system."],"contextual_background":[],"source_references":["Original rulebook p7 Destiny","Original rulebook p7 illustrated special destiny card, extraction lines603–612."]}},{"id":"Q166","question":{"id":"Q166","question":"For the Fido flare effect specifically described in the official FAQ as forcing a player to draw from the discard pile, does the card come from the top of that pile, at random, or from a freely chosen position?"},"key":{"id":"Q166","required_facts":["The forced draw described by the FAQ takes the top card of the discard pile."],"contextual_background":["The source calls this Fido flare without identifying Wild versus Super. No full trigger, role, phase, target-selection permission, cost or remaining effect is supplied."],"source_references":["2018 FAQ p4 extraction lines280–287, Fido flare described as forcing a top-discard draw."]}}],"unchanged_entry_bindings":[{"id":"Q001","question_sha256":"4608070a1636d213d228b9a68a2932672417b14881f936bf950a4af393ffff13","key_sha256":"a432ca0462ab65402ab11f0b477028ff3b65734adc987dfdb9bc23e392c8d207"},{"id":"Q002","question_sha256":"8b13cb8b5cfd8b74b92064062c4c25cd866b5c1a6aba6f901e31108c0672fdcc","key_sha256":"56e230748180ce56aff53e67097